      "side": 1,
      "message": "For followup CL:\n\n**Unprotected Integer Overflow in Offset Calculation** In the new `get_frame` function, there is a vulnerability when shifting the offset for specific capture types:\n\n```c\n\tif (skip_image_offset(global_context.current_capture_type))\n\t\toffset +\u003d FP_SENSOR_IMAGE_OFFSET;\n\n```\n\nBecause `offset` is a `uint32_t` provided by the caller (ultimately derived from host commands), adding `FP_SENSOR_IMAGE_OFFSET` without bounds checking can cause `offset` to wrap around to a very small number (e.g., `UINT32_MAX + 10` becomes `9`).\n\nIf this happens, the wrapped `offset` will easily pass the subsequent `validate_fp_buffer_offset` check. The host will then successfully read memory from the beginning of `fp_buffer` rather than receiving an out-of-bounds error.",
